# AmorphDB PWA — myapp Setup
#
# Initializes the app's data structure and defines the per-user watcher
# registration procedure called by the reference signup watcher
# (auth/signup.mbl).
#
# `amorphctl init-pwa` generates this file. Edit it to fit the
# application — token lifetime, per-user watchers, app-wide watchers
# and procedures all live here.
#
# After deployment the app subtree looks like:
#   world.apps.myapp.app       - shared UI configuration
#   world.apps.myapp.auth      - app-defined credentials
#   world.apps.myapp.tokens    - active auth tokens
#   world.apps.myapp.devices   - pre-auth browser connections
#   world.apps.myapp.users     - per-user data subtrees

# Token lifetime in seconds. 0 disables expiry.
# 604800 = 7 days.
world.apps.myapp.app._token_ttl = 604800

# my.app.setup_user_watchers is called by auth/signup.mbl after a new
# user is created and their data subtree (world.apps.myapp.users[username])
# is materialized, but before the auto-login token is issued. Register
# per-user watchers here so each user's reactive logic is live by the
# time their first authenticated request arrives.
#
# A typical pattern: a logout watcher that removes the user's tokens
# when they signal logout intent. Replace or extend with app-specific
# behavior as the application grows.

procedure my.app.setup_user_watchers(username):

    # Per-user logout. Removes every token whose .identity matches this
    # user, then quietly resets the intent so the watcher does not loop.
    # The next authenticated request from any device for this user will
    # fail resolveAuth and the boilerplate's 401 handling (Step B5)
    # will route the browser back to the login screen.
    watch my.app.logout_handler[username](
            world.apps.myapp.users[username].intent.logout):
        if world.apps.myapp.users[username].intent.logout = true:
            for token in world.apps.myapp.tokens:
                if token.identity = username:
                    token = unknown
            world.apps.myapp.users[username].intent.logout = (quietly) false

    # Add additional per-user watchers below as the app grows. Each
    # watcher should observe paths under
    # world.apps.myapp.users[username].* and react to user-driven
    # intents. Use my.app.<name>[username] watcher names so each user
    # gets a distinct, named watcher instance.
    pass
